The formula for the cosine of the angle $\theta$ between two vectors $\vec{u}$ and $\vec{v}$ is \begin{align*}
\cos \theta & = \frac{\vec{u} \cdot \vec{v}}{\left\lVert\vec{u}\right\rVert \left\lVert\vec{v}\right\rVert}.
\end{align*}
Using this formula with $\vec{u} = \vec{AB}$ and $\vec{v} = \vec{BC}$, we get
\begin{align*}
\cos \angle ABC & = \frac{\begin{pmatrix} 2\\7\\-1 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} -5\\5\\-2 \end{pmatrix}}{\left\lVert\begin{pmatrix} 2\\7\\-1 \end{pmatrix}\right\rVert \left\lVert\begin{pmatrix} -5\\5\\-2 \end{pmatrix}\right\rVert} \\
