Since $1000 = 2^3 \cdot 5^3$, and $997 = 2^0 \cdot 7 \cdot 71$, it has no common factors with $1000$ except $1$. This means that $\gcd(997,1000) = 1$, which implies that $997$ has an inverse modulo $1000$.

